binPol(RingElement,ZZ,ZZ) -- product of two binomial polynomials
****************************************************************

  * Function: *note binPol: binPol_lpRingElement_cmZZ_cmZZ_rp,
  * Usage: 
        binPol(d,n,i)
  * Inputs:
      * d, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the variable of
        the polynomial ring
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, in [0,n]
  * Outputs:
      * a polynomial taking integers to integers

Description
===========

The polynomial of degree <= n, with values 0 for all d in [-n,0]-{-i} and with
value (-1)^i when d = -i.
+-------------------+
|i1 : QQ[d]         |
|                   |
|o1 = QQ[d]         |
|                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing|
+-------------------+
|i2 : binPol(d,3,1) |
|                   |
|     1 3   5 2     |
|o2 = -d  + -d  + 3d|
|     2     2       |
|                   |
|o2 : QQ[d]         |
+-------------------+

See also
========

  * *note hilbPol: hilbPol_lpRingElement_cmZZ_cmList_cmList_rp, -- Hilbert
    polynomial

