Triplet -- triplet
******************

Description
===========

A Triplet is a list consisting of three degree sequences, each  of which is a
list of increasing integers. These three degree sequences fulfill certain
compatibility conditions. There are two different but equivalent versions:


1. A degree triplet, see Definition 2.9 in math.AC/1207.2071 "Triplets of pure
free squarefree complexes"


2. A homology triplet, see Definition 5.4 in math.AC/1212.3675 "Zipping Tate
resolutions and exterior coalgebras"


The routines *note isDegreeTriplet: isDegreeTriplet_lpTriplet_rp, and *note
isHomologyTriplet: isHomologyTriplet_lpTriplet_rp, checks if a triplet fulfills
the compatibility conditions for degree and homology triplets, respectively.
The routine *note toHomology: toHomology_lpTriplet_rp, converts from a degree
triplet to a homology triplet, and the routine *note toDegree:
toDegree_lpTriplet_rp, converts from a homology triplet to a degree triplet.

Functions and methods returning an object of class Triplet:
===========================================================

  * "rotBack" -- see *note rotBack(Triplet): rotBack_lpTriplet_rp, -- backward
    cyclic permutation
  * "rotForw" -- see *note rotForw(Triplet): rotForw_lpTriplet_rp, -- forward
    cyclic permutation
  * "toDegree" -- see *note toDegree(Triplet): toDegree_lpTriplet_rp, -- from
    homology triplet to degree triplet
  * "toHomology" -- see *note toHomology(Triplet): toHomology_lpTriplet_rp, --
    from degree triplet to homology triplet
  * "triplet" -- see *note triplet(List,List,List):
    triplet_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, -- make a triplet
  * *note triplet(List,List,List): triplet_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, -- make a
    triplet

Methods that use an object of class Triplet:
============================================

  * *note Betti1(Triplet): Betti1_lpTriplet_rp, -- Betti numbers of first pure
    complex
  * *note Betti3(Triplet): Betti3_lpTriplet_rp, -- Betti numbers of the three
    pure complexes
  * *note BettiDiagram1(Triplet): BettiDiagram1_lpTriplet_rp, -- Betti diagram
    of first pure complex
  * *note BettiDiagram3(Triplet): BettiDiagram3_lpTriplet_rp, -- Betti diagrams
    of the three pure complexes
  * *note cohMatrix(ZZ,ZZ,Triplet): cohMatrix_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmTriplet_rp, --
    cohomology table in matrix form
  * *note cohTable(ZZ,ZZ,Triplet): cohTable_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmTriplet_rp, --
    cohomology table
  * *note dualHomTriplet(Triplet): dualHomTriplet_lpTriplet_rp, -- the dual
    homology triplet
  * *note hilbCoeff(Triplet): hilbCoeff_lpTriplet_rp, -- coefficients of
    Hilbert polynomial
  * *note isDegreeTriplet(Triplet): isDegreeTriplet_lpTriplet_rp, -- checks if
    it is a degree triplet
  * *note isHomologyTriplet(Triplet): isHomologyTriplet_lpTriplet_rp, -- checks
    if it is a homology triplet
  * *note rotBack(Triplet): rotBack_lpTriplet_rp, -- backward cyclic
    permutation
  * *note rotForw(Triplet): rotForw_lpTriplet_rp, -- forward cyclic permutation
  * *note toDegree(Triplet): toDegree_lpTriplet_rp, -- from homology triplet to
    degree triplet
  * *note toHomology(Triplet): toHomology_lpTriplet_rp, -- from degree triplet
    to homology triplet
  * *note type(Triplet): type_lpTriplet_rp, -- number of variables

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Triplet: Triplet, is a *note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with
ancestor classes *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, < *note VisibleList:
(Macaulay2Doc)VisibleList, < *note BasicList: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList, < *note
Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

